<article class="page wrap reading">
  <h1>Your clients' documents stay yours.</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">Elder law files hold the most sensitive information a family has. We built DossierIQ with that in mind, and we'll only tell you what's true today.</p>

  <h2>Where documents live</h2>
  <p>Documents are stored in your firm's own Google Drive or SharePoint, not in a DossierIQ warehouse.</p>

  <h2>Sharing, with a record</h2>
  <p>Clean Room links expire, require a one-time code, and record every view and download in a tamper-evident log. Files can be watermarked and download-limited.</p>

  <h2>Authority before access</h2>
  <p>Sensitive discovery steps, like connecting a client's mailbox, require a recorded statement of the firm's authority first.</p>

  <h2>Backups</h2>
  <p>Every night the DossierIQ server and database are backed up, encrypted, and copied off-site, in addition to daily, weekly and monthly copies kept locally. We've verified those off-site backups can be recovered.</p>

  <h2>Encryption at rest for connections</h2>
  <p>The keys DossierIQ uses to reach your storage are encrypted at rest.</p>

  <h2>Credentials are never shared</h2>
  <p>Documents marked as login credentials can't be sent through a share link or included in downloads.</p>

  <h2>Your data isn't for sale</h2>
  <p>We don't sell your data. Not your firm's, not your clients'.</p>

  <h2>What DossierIQ is and isn't</h2>
  <p>DossierIQ organizes and flags; attorneys and staff confirm. It's guidance, not legal advice. PASI is a software company, not a law firm.</p>

  <p class="fine end">Questions about how DossierIQ handles data? Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we'll walk you through it. Read the <a href="{{ site.privacyUrl }}">privacy notice</a>.</p>
</article>
